1
00:01:33,060 --> 00:01:38,250
[First Love Again]

2
00:01:38,460 --> 00:01:40,990
[Episode 15]

3
00:01:48,310 --> 00:01:49,430
I remember before I went on stage,

4
00:01:49,430 --> 00:01:51,090
I kept memorizing the script.

5
00:01:51,560 --> 00:01:52,400
I'm certain that number

6
00:01:52,400 --> 00:01:54,150
was written on the script.

7
00:02:01,710 --> 00:02:02,840
Please do me a favor.

8
00:02:03,590 --> 00:02:04,680
You can't just check

9
00:02:04,680 --> 00:02:06,560
the surveillance footage
whenever you want.

10
00:02:06,560 --> 00:02:07,530
If you want to check it,

11
00:02:07,530 --> 00:02:10,330
you need to get the approval slip
from the college.

12
00:02:10,430 --> 00:02:12,200
Can you make an exception this once?

13
00:02:12,200 --> 00:02:13,190
No.

14
00:02:13,280 --> 00:02:15,150
We have principles in our work.

15
00:02:16,120 --> 00:02:17,150
I'm really in a hurry.

16
00:02:17,150 --> 00:02:18,220
Can you just do it this once?

17
00:02:18,220 --> 00:02:18,850
Please.

18
00:02:19,079 --> 00:02:19,910
Hello, sir.

19
00:02:20,270 --> 00:02:21,590
Here is the approval slip
I just got from the office.

20
00:02:21,590 --> 00:02:22,360
Take a look.

21
00:02:26,550 --> 00:02:27,960
You two are together?

22
00:02:33,490 --> 00:02:34,079
Yes.

23
00:02:34,340 --> 00:02:35,730
We are together.

24
00:02:35,870 --> 00:02:37,520
I asked him to come to you first,

25
00:02:37,520 --> 00:02:39,780
while I went to the office
to get the slip.

26
00:02:40,960 --> 00:02:42,990
With the slip, of course you can check.

27
00:02:42,990 --> 00:02:44,550
How long do you need?

28
00:02:45,870 --> 00:02:46,550
It'll be quick.

29
00:02:46,550 --> 00:02:47,150
Yes.

30
00:02:48,040 --> 00:02:49,960
I have to hand over my shift
early tomorrow morning.

31
00:02:49,960 --> 00:02:50,800
Make it quick.

32
00:02:51,590 --> 00:02:52,320
Don't worry.

33
00:02:52,480 --> 00:02:54,200
We definitely won't cause you any trouble.

34
00:02:54,200 --> 00:02:54,800
Okay.

35
00:02:58,050 --> 00:02:59,700
Sir, please take this.

36
00:02:59,980 --> 00:03:00,920
-Don't.
-No. No.

37
00:03:00,920 --> 00:03:01,640
No, no, no.

38
00:03:01,640 --> 00:03:03,040
Sorry to trouble you for opening up
for us so late.

39
00:03:03,040 --> 00:03:03,960
Thank you.

40
00:03:05,150 --> 00:03:06,390
What a polite kid.

41
00:03:06,670 --> 00:03:07,830
Hurry up, go in.

42
00:03:07,870 --> 00:03:08,550
Thank you.

43
00:03:08,580 --> 00:03:09,180
Let's go.

44
00:03:11,370 --> 00:03:13,520
[Monitoring Center][Monitoring Room]

45
00:03:13,630 --> 00:03:15,800
[Jiangcheng University]

46
00:03:14,390 --> 00:03:14,990
Here we go.

47
00:03:15,180 --> 00:03:17,380
Don't skip anything. Watch carefully.

48
00:03:19,140 --> 00:03:20,430
[June 28, 2019]

49
00:03:22,200 --> 00:03:25,079
[June 28, 2019]

50
00:03:22,660 --> 00:03:23,720
Take a look at this.

51
00:03:25,079 --> 00:03:26,360
[June 28, 2019]

52
00:03:28,280 --> 00:03:29,410
[June 28, 2019]

53
00:03:29,079 --> 00:03:29,829
Zoom in.

54
00:03:35,990 --> 00:03:36,670
This angle doesn't work.

55
00:03:36,670 --> 00:03:37,590
Try another angle.

56
00:03:36,780 --> 00:03:37,880
[June 28, 2019] [CAM 09010]

57
00:03:41,920 --> 00:03:43,079
I said let's change the angle.

58
00:03:43,079 --> 00:03:45,140
We can't see clearly from this angle.

59
00:03:45,550 --> 00:03:47,079
Don't rush. Take your time.

60
00:03:49,079 --> 00:03:49,940
Thank you, sir.

61
00:03:54,240 --> 00:03:54,760
Wait.

62
00:03:54,800 --> 00:03:56,000
Rewind. Rewind a bit.

63
00:03:57,550 --> 00:03:59,240
Why are they all blind spots?

64
00:04:05,990 --> 00:04:06,640
Next.

65
00:04:07,410 --> 00:04:08,670
[June 28, 2019] [CAM 09012]

66
00:04:12,990 --> 00:04:14,670
[Jiangcheng University]

67
00:04:22,270 --> 00:04:24,270
Do you have any more food in your bag?

68
00:04:25,930 --> 00:04:26,520
No.

69
00:04:30,360 --> 00:04:31,040
Keep going.

70
00:04:31,550 --> 00:04:32,330
[June 28, 2019]

71
00:04:32,350 --> 00:04:33,580
[June 28, 2019] [CAM 09011]

72
00:04:35,450 --> 00:04:38,430
[Public Opinion Risk Control]

73
00:04:50,490 --> 00:04:51,400
I found it.

74
00:04:51,630 --> 00:04:52,610
I found it. It's here.

75
00:04:52,610 --> 00:04:53,330
Where?

76
00:04:54,659 --> 00:04:55,270
Here.

77
00:04:56,710 --> 00:04:58,670
Zoom in a bit.

78
00:05:01,850 --> 00:05:02,480
Pause.

79
00:05:02,510 --> 00:05:03,850
Here. Wait a minute.

80
00:05:04,220 --> 00:05:04,830
Here.

81
00:05:08,410 --> 00:05:09,560
Duan Xiaoyu?

82
00:05:14,010 --> 00:05:14,860
Xiaoyu.

83
00:05:15,240 --> 00:05:16,660
Senior, I...

84
00:05:16,690 --> 00:05:17,950
I have something to do.

85
00:05:17,960 --> 00:05:19,030
I'll get going.

86
00:05:26,800 --> 00:05:27,000
[Theme: James's Birthday]

87
00:05:27,000 --> 00:05:27,920
[James tops the list
with over 6.27 million votes]

88
00:05:29,680 --> 00:05:30,720
It really is her.

89
00:05:59,830 --> 00:06:01,290
Why are you looking for me?

90
00:06:04,250 --> 00:06:05,040
What's wrong?

91
00:06:05,040 --> 00:06:06,440
Didn't sleep last night?

92
00:06:11,230 --> 00:06:12,140
What is this?

93
00:06:16,530 --> 00:06:18,870
[June 28, 2019] [CAM 09010]

94
00:06:24,190 --> 00:06:26,540
[June 28, 2019] [CAM 09010]

95
00:06:43,720 --> 00:06:46,620
[Jiangcheng University Campus TV Station]

96
00:07:19,640 --> 00:07:21,620
What are you doing? Feeling guilty?

97
00:07:21,620 --> 00:07:24,220
I have many backups.
You can't delete them all.

98
00:07:25,590 --> 00:07:27,120
Why are you showing me this?

99
00:07:27,760 --> 00:07:29,120
Isn't it obvious?

100
00:07:29,120 --> 00:07:30,230
You swapped out my script,

101
00:07:30,230 --> 00:07:33,150
which caused me to make a mistake
during the competition.

102
00:07:33,150 --> 00:07:34,640
An excellent host

103
00:07:35,590 --> 00:07:38,000
should be able to tell
a faulty script apart.

104
00:07:38,000 --> 00:07:38,790
Besides,

105
00:07:39,000 --> 00:07:40,560
the votes for the All-Star Captain

106
00:07:40,560 --> 00:07:42,000
are all on the official website.

107
00:07:42,000 --> 00:07:43,590
This only shows that you

108
00:07:44,200 --> 00:07:45,860
are not professional enough.

109
00:07:46,800 --> 00:07:49,060
Then thank you for reminding me this way.

110
00:07:50,080 --> 00:07:51,390
Tell me, when we see the director

111
00:07:51,390 --> 00:07:52,640
and other seniors,

112
00:07:53,080 --> 00:07:54,940
should I thank you in front of them,

113
00:07:54,940 --> 00:07:56,670
or will you tell them yourself?

114
00:07:57,440 --> 00:07:58,350
Whatever.

115
00:07:58,909 --> 00:08:01,970
Since I dared to do it,
I'm not afraid of others knowing.

116
00:08:04,560 --> 00:08:06,690
Aren't... Aren't we having a meeting?

117
00:08:20,760 --> 00:08:22,760
I just don't like you. So what?

118
00:08:23,710 --> 00:08:26,240
You, someone with
no professional training,

119
00:08:26,790 --> 00:08:29,230
why do you always get everyone's approval?

120
00:08:31,270 --> 00:08:32,470
Senior Fang Yu...

121
00:08:34,159 --> 00:08:36,159
why is he always looking out for you?

122
00:08:49,960 --> 00:08:51,140
In this interview,

123
00:08:51,320 --> 00:08:53,120
everyone performed quite well.

124
00:08:54,350 --> 00:08:55,870
In a few days, the admission results
from The Starry Sky

125
00:08:55,870 --> 00:08:56,680
will be out.

126
00:08:57,990 --> 00:08:59,230
As I said before,

127
00:09:00,030 --> 00:09:01,460
no matter the result,

128
00:09:01,880 --> 00:09:03,680
let's treat it as an experience.

129
00:09:04,550 --> 00:09:06,150
But some problems

130
00:09:06,630 --> 00:09:08,750
are still worth reviewing carefully.

131
00:09:08,750 --> 00:09:09,990
For example, some students,

132
00:09:09,990 --> 00:09:11,520
when answering questions,

133
00:09:11,630 --> 00:09:13,030
were not fully prepared,

134
00:09:13,340 --> 00:09:15,400
giving utterly ridiculous replies.

135
00:09:15,440 --> 00:09:17,810
Others were not familiar enough
with their scripts.

136
00:09:17,810 --> 00:09:18,540
You must know

137
00:09:18,990 --> 00:09:20,870
that a broadcast error during a live show

138
00:09:20,870 --> 00:09:22,080
is a major accident.

139
00:09:22,700 --> 00:09:24,160
So if you want to become

140
00:09:24,160 --> 00:09:26,280
a qualified professional host,

141
00:09:26,960 --> 00:09:28,560
we still have a long way to go.

142
00:09:29,200 --> 00:09:32,200
We must keep improving
our professional competence.

143
00:09:47,710 --> 00:09:48,560
Xiangxiang.

144
00:09:48,800 --> 00:09:51,080
Duan Xiaoyu's behaviour was completely
out of line.

145
00:09:51,080 --> 00:09:53,080
Why didn't you report her on the spot?

146
00:09:53,080 --> 00:09:53,710
Yeah.

147
00:09:53,710 --> 00:09:56,110
It's not the first time
she's targeted you.

148
00:09:56,280 --> 00:09:59,210
If you hesitate,
trouble will come back to haunt you.

149
00:09:59,230 --> 00:10:01,630
Who knows what she might do to you
next time.

150
00:10:03,040 --> 00:10:05,470
Actually, I almost said it.

151
00:10:05,800 --> 00:10:07,260
Then why did you soften up?

152
00:10:08,080 --> 00:10:09,610
It's not that I softened up.

153
00:10:09,870 --> 00:10:11,800
I just thought that if this got out,

154
00:10:11,870 --> 00:10:14,800
it could have very serious consequences.

155
00:10:15,080 --> 00:10:16,040
What consequences?

156
00:10:16,040 --> 00:10:17,080
For Duan Xiaoyu?

157
00:10:18,280 --> 00:10:19,160
Think about it.

158
00:10:19,230 --> 00:10:22,110
Although I can't intern
at this program anymore,

159
00:10:22,280 --> 00:10:24,080
if the truth comes out,

160
00:10:24,110 --> 00:10:26,160
Duan Xiaoyu will be completely ruined.

161
00:10:26,160 --> 00:10:27,890
Who else would dare to hire her?

162
00:10:28,710 --> 00:10:29,560
Besides,

163
00:10:29,870 --> 00:10:31,710
her father is also a host.

164
00:10:32,350 --> 00:10:34,080
If The Starry Sky finds out about this,

165
00:10:34,080 --> 00:10:35,710
it will definitely become news.

166
00:10:35,710 --> 00:10:37,470
Her dad will definitely be
dragged into it.

167
00:10:37,470 --> 00:10:39,930
Family members are always innocent, right?

168
00:10:40,080 --> 00:10:42,320
But Duan Xiaoyu did it.

169
00:10:42,320 --> 00:10:43,560
She didn't consider
the consequences herself.

170
00:10:43,560 --> 00:10:45,620
Why should you consider them for her?

171
00:10:46,590 --> 00:10:49,110
I was really angry at first too.

172
00:10:49,470 --> 00:10:51,330
Do you know what she told me today?

173
00:10:52,350 --> 00:10:54,160
She said she kept picking on me

174
00:10:54,160 --> 00:10:56,080
because everyone praises me,

175
00:10:56,080 --> 00:10:58,080
and Senior Fang Yu treats me so well.

176
00:10:58,950 --> 00:11:00,140
That's it?

177
00:11:00,990 --> 00:11:02,830
She changed the script over that?

178
00:11:02,830 --> 00:11:04,080
So childish.

179
00:11:05,560 --> 00:11:07,400
So, if you think about it,

180
00:11:07,470 --> 00:11:08,350
she's really just

181
00:11:08,350 --> 00:11:09,870
a spoiled rich girl.

182
00:11:10,470 --> 00:11:12,150
Two words sum her up:

183
00:11:12,230 --> 00:11:13,090
princess syndrome.

184
00:11:13,090 --> 00:11:15,020
Yes, exactly. Princess syndrome.

185
00:11:15,390 --> 00:11:17,160
It's cooked. Dig in.

186
00:11:19,590 --> 00:11:20,200
Come.

187
00:11:30,320 --> 00:11:31,160
As the NBA

188
00:11:31,160 --> 00:11:33,350
All‑Star voting rules keep evolving,

189
00:11:33,350 --> 00:11:35,870
the All-Star vote counts
keep being refreshed

190
00:11:35,870 --> 00:11:37,160
and surpassed.

191
00:11:37,160 --> 00:11:38,680
As of 2018,

192
00:11:53,830 --> 00:11:56,110
with over 3.15 million votes,

193
00:11:56,200 --> 00:11:57,630
he ranks

194
00:11:58,230 --> 00:12:00,440
second in history as the vote king.

195
00:12:00,800 --> 00:12:01,530
Xiangxiang,

196
00:12:03,040 --> 00:12:03,920
take a break.

197
00:12:06,160 --> 00:12:07,230
Senior.

198
00:12:08,110 --> 00:12:09,960
Gu told me he has a good friend

199
00:12:09,960 --> 00:12:12,040
who encountered some
professional problems,

200
00:12:12,040 --> 00:12:13,770
and insisted I come talk to you.

201
00:12:17,130 --> 00:12:17,930
You guys talk.

202
00:12:25,030 --> 00:12:25,860
Senior.

203
00:12:26,440 --> 00:12:28,640
You must already know about my problem.

204
00:12:29,800 --> 00:12:31,080
I'm really sorry.

205
00:12:31,160 --> 00:12:33,280
Last time you taught me not to be nervous,

206
00:12:33,280 --> 00:12:34,230
but on stage,

207
00:12:34,230 --> 00:12:36,080
when I really encountered a problem,

208
00:12:36,080 --> 00:12:37,340
I still couldn't do it.

209
00:12:41,590 --> 00:12:42,200
Come.

210
00:12:46,280 --> 00:12:47,740
Do you want to hear a story?

211
00:12:52,160 --> 00:12:54,440
I once had a fellow host colleague

212
00:12:55,750 --> 00:12:58,220
who joined the station
around the same time as me.

213
00:12:58,220 --> 00:12:59,480
When he first arrived,

214
00:12:59,870 --> 00:13:02,160
because he wasn't professionally trained,

215
00:13:02,160 --> 00:13:04,110
he'd often mispronounce words

216
00:13:04,510 --> 00:13:05,770
and get numbers wrong.

217
00:13:06,470 --> 00:13:09,200
I remember our station had a clear rule:

218
00:13:09,280 --> 00:13:10,510
fifty‑yuan fine

219
00:13:11,750 --> 00:13:13,080
for every misread word.

220
00:13:15,630 --> 00:13:17,330
I remember this colleague

221
00:13:17,710 --> 00:13:20,440
had his entire month's salary
deducted one month

222
00:13:21,400 --> 00:13:23,660
and even owed the station dozens of yuan.

223
00:13:25,630 --> 00:13:27,280
But he didn't get discouraged

224
00:13:27,280 --> 00:13:28,480
or give up on himself.

225
00:13:29,680 --> 00:13:32,680
Instead, he worked even harder
preparing his scripts.

226
00:13:32,680 --> 00:13:34,110
Sometimes he wouldn't sleep,

227
00:13:34,110 --> 00:13:36,370
reading the scripts over and over again.

228
00:13:36,870 --> 00:13:38,210
For the next few years,

229
00:13:38,470 --> 00:13:40,590
he was repeatedly honoured

230
00:13:40,960 --> 00:13:43,420
as our show's zero‑error outstanding host.

231
00:13:50,160 --> 00:13:51,320
I always felt

232
00:13:52,800 --> 00:13:54,260
that dreams were far away.

233
00:13:55,030 --> 00:13:56,140
But I know that

234
00:13:56,590 --> 00:13:58,230
as long as we stay grounded,

235
00:13:58,800 --> 00:14:01,200
we will get one step closer to our dreams.

236
00:14:03,920 --> 00:14:05,160
Failure is not scary.

237
00:14:05,800 --> 00:14:07,080
Just start over.

238
00:14:09,470 --> 00:14:10,710
Gu told me

239
00:14:10,800 --> 00:14:12,930
that you are not a broadcasting major.

240
00:14:14,510 --> 00:14:16,970
Yet you still got into
the campus TV station.

241
00:14:17,320 --> 00:14:19,520
That proves you've got real potential.

242
00:14:23,510 --> 00:14:24,680
You messed up this round

243
00:14:24,680 --> 00:14:26,080
and didn't get selected.

244
00:14:26,080 --> 00:14:28,200
Next, let's sum up the experience

245
00:14:28,350 --> 00:14:29,610
and keep working hard.

246
00:14:29,800 --> 00:14:31,730
I believe you can definitely do it.

247
00:14:33,710 --> 00:14:35,040
You're only a freshman.

248
00:14:35,320 --> 00:14:36,980
You still have a long way to go.

249
00:14:41,320 --> 00:14:42,800
Thank you, Senior.

250
00:14:43,960 --> 00:14:45,560
I will definitely work hard.

251
00:15:06,400 --> 00:15:07,280
Hello.

252
00:15:08,350 --> 00:15:10,630
Is this Zhou Xiangxiang?

253
00:15:11,630 --> 00:15:14,430
This is the "24s" program team
from The Starry Sky.

254
00:15:14,750 --> 00:15:15,610
Yes, speaking.

255
00:15:16,960 --> 00:15:17,830
Here's the thing.

256
00:15:17,830 --> 00:15:19,110
After the last assessment,

257
00:15:19,110 --> 00:15:20,870
we have been evaluating the results.

258
00:15:20,870 --> 00:15:22,280
Considering your overall performance,

259
00:15:22,280 --> 00:15:24,160
we hope you can take a make-up test.

260
00:15:24,160 --> 00:15:25,920
It will be this Friday afternoon.

261
00:15:25,920 --> 00:15:26,980
Are you available?

262
00:15:29,080 --> 00:15:30,160
Yes, I am.

263
00:15:30,350 --> 00:15:31,230
See you then.

264
00:15:34,990 --> 00:15:35,850
What happened?

265
00:15:36,510 --> 00:15:39,040
The Starry Sky notified me
to take a make-up test.

266
00:15:39,040 --> 00:15:40,570
That's great news.

267
00:15:40,680 --> 00:15:42,680
When one door shuts, another opens.

268
00:15:42,680 --> 00:15:44,230
We should celebrate. Let's go.

269
00:15:44,230 --> 00:15:44,830
Okay.

270
00:15:47,160 --> 00:15:48,990
See? I told you you'd be fine.

271
00:15:50,800 --> 00:15:51,830
Um...

272
00:15:53,040 --> 00:15:54,080
Let's talk.

273
00:15:56,380 --> 00:15:57,900
I'll wait for you up ahead.

274
00:16:04,920 --> 00:16:05,560
Go ahead.

275
00:16:08,080 --> 00:16:08,830
Did you

276
00:16:09,440 --> 00:16:11,560
get the call from "24s"?

277
00:16:13,280 --> 00:16:14,990
Did you do something?

278
00:16:16,160 --> 00:16:17,280
Not much.

279
00:16:17,870 --> 00:16:20,590
I went to see the campus TV station
leaders this morning.

280
00:16:20,590 --> 00:16:21,800
I told them

281
00:16:22,000 --> 00:16:24,660
that when I was preparing
the script materials,

282
00:16:24,720 --> 00:16:26,780
I accidentally typed the wrong data,

283
00:16:27,960 --> 00:16:30,750
printed it out without checking,

284
00:16:31,230 --> 00:16:32,960
and gave you the wrong script.

285
00:16:34,400 --> 00:16:35,630
After they found out,

286
00:16:36,110 --> 00:16:38,830
they reported it to The Starry Sky
for you.

287
00:16:46,400 --> 00:16:48,000
Did your conscience kick in?

288
00:16:48,350 --> 00:16:50,040
Don't be so harsh.

289
00:16:50,990 --> 00:16:52,850
Our campus TV station only has
this one chance.

290
00:16:52,850 --> 00:16:55,180
I want to compete with you
fair and square.

291
00:16:59,160 --> 00:16:59,830
Alright.

292
00:17:00,110 --> 00:17:01,910
Go prepare for the second round.

293
00:17:02,040 --> 00:17:03,040
I'm leaving.

294
00:17:15,710 --> 00:17:17,680
''24s'' notified me
to take a make-up test.

295
00:17:17,680 --> 00:17:19,210
I want to treat you to a meal.

296
00:17:21,119 --> 00:17:21,849
Xiangxiang.

297
00:17:22,920 --> 00:17:23,599
Senior.

298
00:17:23,990 --> 00:17:24,790
Congratulations.

299
00:17:24,790 --> 00:17:27,270
I just heard you're going to
take the make-up test.

300
00:17:27,270 --> 00:17:28,870
I was just about to thank you.

301
00:17:29,030 --> 00:17:29,680
If you guys hadn't

302
00:17:29,680 --> 00:17:31,740
stayed up late checking the footage,

303
00:17:31,770 --> 00:17:34,470
I don't think Duan Xiaoyu
would've owned up to it.

304
00:17:34,470 --> 00:17:35,400
You really saved me.

305
00:17:35,400 --> 00:17:36,550
Don't say that.

306
00:17:36,550 --> 00:17:38,280
We're good friends, aren't we?

307
00:17:40,120 --> 00:17:42,520
By the way,
I just asked Gu Han out for a meal.

308
00:17:42,680 --> 00:17:43,470
Are you free?

309
00:17:43,510 --> 00:17:44,710
I want to treat both of you together

310
00:17:44,710 --> 00:17:45,910
to show my gratitude.

311
00:17:48,790 --> 00:17:50,750
Today might not work.

312
00:17:51,230 --> 00:17:53,360
I have to go to the city TV station
in a bit.

313
00:17:53,360 --> 00:17:53,960
Listen,

314
00:17:54,210 --> 00:17:56,140
don't worry about the meal for now.

315
00:17:56,330 --> 00:17:57,890
Just prepare well for the make-up test.

316
00:17:57,890 --> 00:17:59,490
I'll wait for your good news.

317
00:17:59,840 --> 00:18:00,440
Okay.

318
00:18:01,200 --> 00:18:02,710
I'll get going then.

319
00:18:03,840 --> 00:18:04,440
Good luck.

320
00:18:04,990 --> 00:18:05,600
Bye bye.

321
00:18:12,730 --> 00:18:13,890
[Gu Han]

322
00:18:13,000 --> 00:18:14,460
Great, congratulations.

323
00:18:31,280 --> 00:18:32,080
That happy?

324
00:18:33,790 --> 00:18:35,720
I thought I had no chance at all.

325
00:18:35,880 --> 00:18:37,810
But my luck finally turned around.

326
00:18:50,520 --> 00:18:51,320
What's wrong?

327
00:18:54,870 --> 00:18:57,790
Even though I got the chance
to take the make-up test,

328
00:18:57,790 --> 00:19:00,310
if something unexpected happens again,

329
00:19:01,010 --> 00:19:03,030
I don't know if I'll get nervous.

330
00:19:03,160 --> 00:19:04,400
I'm really unsure.

331
00:19:21,960 --> 00:19:23,880
Didn't Fang Yu teach you?

332
00:19:26,470 --> 00:19:27,790
He taught me a lot,

333
00:19:28,610 --> 00:19:30,720
but it doesn't seem to suit me.

334
00:19:39,070 --> 00:19:41,600
The make-up test is about basketball,
right?

335
00:19:58,930 --> 00:20:03,460
[Service]

336
00:20:01,810 --> 00:20:02,410
Thank you.

337
00:20:05,120 --> 00:20:06,380
What are we doing here?

338
00:20:11,310 --> 00:20:11,920
Let's go.

339
00:20:15,710 --> 00:20:17,110
What are we going to play?

340
00:20:24,680 --> 00:20:25,840
Almost, almost.

341
00:20:26,640 --> 00:20:27,640
Almost.

342
00:20:28,230 --> 00:20:29,560
Turn right, turn right.

343
00:20:35,640 --> 00:20:36,230
Come on.

344
00:20:36,460 --> 00:20:38,540
Shooting hoops isn't on my test.

345
00:20:39,170 --> 00:20:40,830
Just two rounds then we leave.

346
00:20:48,960 --> 00:20:49,550
Come on.

347
00:20:51,400 --> 00:20:53,600
Interactive Park weekend promotion.

348
00:20:53,600 --> 00:20:55,920
Great deals. Buy ten, get one free.

349
00:20:58,070 --> 00:20:58,800
How about it?

350
00:20:58,880 --> 00:21:01,200
Interactive Park weekend promotion.

351
00:21:01,200 --> 00:21:03,600
Great deals. Buy ten, get one free.

352
00:21:15,440 --> 00:21:16,640
Airball.

353
00:21:16,640 --> 00:21:18,230
Seriously?

354
00:21:18,440 --> 00:21:19,880
Even adults shoot that badly?

355
00:21:19,880 --> 00:21:21,710
That was terrible!

356
00:21:22,310 --> 00:21:23,120
No, you can't do that.

357
00:21:23,120 --> 00:21:24,270
Exactly.

358
00:21:25,070 --> 00:21:26,790
-You can't even make a shot.
-Time's almost up.

359
00:21:26,790 --> 00:21:28,690
No way. You can't make it.

360
00:21:29,710 --> 00:21:31,500
She's shooting terribly.

361
00:21:31,520 --> 00:21:32,120
So bad.

362
00:21:32,120 --> 00:21:33,980
Don't be distracted. Keep going.

363
00:21:34,880 --> 00:21:36,160
She's worse than you three.

364
00:21:36,160 --> 00:21:37,860
Not even as good as me.

365
00:21:43,270 --> 00:21:45,000
Even an adult shoots like that.

366
00:21:45,550 --> 00:21:46,750
Can't even make it.

367
00:21:46,750 --> 00:21:47,990
Missed again.

368
00:21:50,030 --> 00:21:51,300
I don't want to shoot.

369
00:21:53,900 --> 00:21:54,560
Look ahead.

370
00:21:56,650 --> 00:21:57,710
Take a deep breath.

371
00:21:58,840 --> 00:22:00,410
I'd do better than her.

372
00:22:02,310 --> 00:22:02,910
Come on.

373
00:22:04,210 --> 00:22:05,260
Airball.

374
00:22:26,120 --> 00:22:26,710
Shoot.

375
00:22:41,840 --> 00:22:42,440
It went in.

376
00:23:05,600 --> 00:23:06,880
Give me, give me, give me!

377
00:23:06,880 --> 00:23:08,320
-Here.
-And me too.

378
00:23:08,470 --> 00:23:09,160
Good job.

379
00:23:09,200 --> 00:23:09,880
I want one too.

380
00:23:09,880 --> 00:23:11,160
-Let's go.
-Let's go play.

381
00:23:11,160 --> 00:23:12,020
Thank you, sir.

382
00:23:21,920 --> 00:23:23,600
Thank you, Coach Gu.

383
00:23:23,990 --> 00:23:25,250
Why do you call me that?

384
00:23:25,510 --> 00:23:28,640
Because you have your unique
Gu-style training method.

385
00:23:29,200 --> 00:23:32,730
I'm auditioning to be a host
and you let me practice my shooting.

386
00:23:33,680 --> 00:23:34,790
What kind of dance is this guy doing?

387
00:23:34,790 --> 00:23:35,850
It looks terrible.

388
00:23:37,320 --> 00:23:38,300
Look at that boy.

389
00:23:43,800 --> 00:23:46,200
There are a lot of onlookers here
every day.

390
00:23:46,230 --> 00:23:46,880
Actually,

391
00:23:47,320 --> 00:23:49,360
he's just like you
when you were shooting.

392
00:23:49,360 --> 00:23:51,560
People might laugh at him at any moment,

393
00:23:51,720 --> 00:23:53,780
yet he doesn't let it
get to him at all.

394
00:23:54,150 --> 00:23:55,900
Because he focuses on himself.

395
00:23:56,470 --> 00:23:57,670
He enjoys the moment.

396
00:23:58,870 --> 00:23:59,830
You mean

397
00:24:00,400 --> 00:24:02,460
there's uncertainty in everything.

398
00:24:03,840 --> 00:24:05,290
Deep down you already know,

399
00:24:05,290 --> 00:24:06,960
you're fully capable of hosting,

400
00:24:06,960 --> 00:24:07,550
right?

401
00:24:08,590 --> 00:24:09,900
But whenever you run into trouble,

402
00:24:09,900 --> 00:24:10,920
or something unexpected happens,

403
00:24:10,920 --> 00:24:11,850
you get nervous.

404
00:24:12,400 --> 00:24:14,120
This isn't a problem
with your professionalism.

405
00:24:14,120 --> 00:24:15,580
It's a psychological one.

406
00:24:17,920 --> 00:24:19,360
Just like when we play

407
00:24:19,960 --> 00:24:21,200
away games.

408
00:24:21,490 --> 00:24:23,150
Every time I step up
to the free‑throw line,

409
00:24:23,150 --> 00:24:24,560
opposing fans in the stands

410
00:24:24,560 --> 00:24:26,230
wave those cheering sticks like crazy,

411
00:24:26,230 --> 00:24:27,560
trying to throw you off.

412
00:24:27,600 --> 00:24:29,600
Sometimes they even shout insults.

413
00:24:30,360 --> 00:24:32,290
Do you know what I'm thinking then?

414
00:24:33,960 --> 00:24:35,620
I don't think about anything.

415
00:24:36,500 --> 00:24:38,600
All I need to do is take the shot.

416
00:24:40,160 --> 00:24:41,760
I believe you can do the same.

417
00:24:41,910 --> 00:24:42,840
You've got this.

418
00:24:59,660 --> 00:25:01,120
[The Starry Sky]

419
00:25:01,120 --> 00:25:03,090
[Live Sports]

420
00:25:04,710 --> 00:25:10,760
[Toilet]

421
00:25:22,700 --> 00:25:24,280
[The Starry Sky]

422
00:25:32,610 --> 00:25:33,670
Stand by.

423
00:25:34,200 --> 00:25:37,460
Three, two, one, action.

424
00:25:35,130 --> 00:25:36,860
[The Starry Sky]

425
00:25:36,930 --> 00:25:43,130
[Filming]

426
00:25:37,960 --> 00:25:39,200
Jump as your heart leads.

427
00:25:39,200 --> 00:25:40,440
Shoot for your dreams.

428
00:25:40,440 --> 00:25:41,070
Hello, everyone.

429
00:25:41,070 --> 00:25:42,680
I'm Zhou Xiangxiang,

430
00:25:42,680 --> 00:25:43,610
host of ''24s''.

431
00:25:43,640 --> 00:25:45,790
Today's halftime interactive segment is:

432
00:25:45,710 --> 00:25:46,070
[The Starry Sky] [Host: Zhou Xiangxiang]

433
00:25:45,920 --> 00:25:48,300
Share Your Basketball Story.

434
00:25:46,120 --> 00:25:47,270
[The Starry Sky]

435
00:25:47,320 --> 00:25:47,880
[Halftime Interaction:
Share Your Basketball Story]

436
00:25:48,400 --> 00:25:49,610
Not bad, Xiangxiang.

437
00:25:49,710 --> 00:25:50,960
She turned the tide

438
00:25:50,960 --> 00:25:52,420
and made a buzzer-beater.

439
00:25:52,520 --> 00:25:53,500
Of course.

440
00:25:53,760 --> 00:25:54,940
After all, she had help

441
00:25:54,940 --> 00:25:56,450
from a clutch player.

442
00:25:57,680 --> 00:25:58,270
Go.

443
00:26:04,640 --> 00:26:06,160
You know, someone

444
00:26:06,160 --> 00:26:07,840
could just talk to his parents

445
00:26:07,840 --> 00:26:08,950
and easily solve this.

446
00:26:08,950 --> 00:26:11,040
He had to drag others
through a whole ordeal.

447
00:26:11,040 --> 00:26:11,940
So quirky.

448
00:26:15,090 --> 00:26:15,680
Pass!

449
00:26:24,400 --> 00:26:25,070
Nice shot.

450
00:26:32,550 --> 00:26:33,400
What a coincidence.

451
00:26:33,400 --> 00:26:34,790
We even bumped into each other
while eating.

452
00:26:34,790 --> 00:26:35,710
To be honest,

453
00:26:35,710 --> 00:26:36,790
our campus TV station
and your basketball team

454
00:26:36,790 --> 00:26:38,200
have cooperated so many times.

455
00:26:38,200 --> 00:26:39,950
This is the first time we've all
gotten together like this.

456
00:26:39,950 --> 00:26:41,960
We really ought to have a proper feast.

457
00:26:41,960 --> 00:26:44,270
I heard Xiangxiang got accepted
by The Starry Sky.

458
00:26:44,270 --> 00:26:45,440
I told you Xiangxiang

459
00:26:45,440 --> 00:26:46,600
would definitely turn the tables

460
00:26:46,600 --> 00:26:47,710
and make a comeback.

461
00:26:47,710 --> 00:26:48,920
I think she should

462
00:26:48,990 --> 00:26:51,320
treat our Senior Fang to meals
for a month.

463
00:26:52,780 --> 00:26:54,910
Why should she treat Senior Fang to meals
for a month?

464
00:26:54,910 --> 00:26:55,770
You don't know?

465
00:26:56,200 --> 00:26:57,440
Thanks to our Senior Fang,

466
00:26:57,440 --> 00:26:59,200
who pulled an all‑nighter
in the monitoring room

467
00:26:59,200 --> 00:27:00,070
and found out Xiangxiang

468
00:27:00,070 --> 00:27:02,060
had accidentally picked up
Duan Xiaoyu's script.

469
00:27:02,060 --> 00:27:03,060
Hey you,

470
00:27:03,090 --> 00:27:03,700
you media folks,

471
00:27:03,700 --> 00:27:05,990
don't go around taking things
out of context.

472
00:27:05,990 --> 00:27:07,200
It wasn't just Senior Fang

473
00:27:07,200 --> 00:27:08,920
who stayed up all night
in the monitoring room.

474
00:27:08,920 --> 00:27:10,400
He was with Gu Han,

475
00:27:10,400 --> 00:27:12,030
reviewing the footage together,
all night long.

476
00:27:12,030 --> 00:27:12,640
Got it?

477
00:27:15,440 --> 00:27:16,640
Sirui is right.

478
00:27:16,920 --> 00:27:17,890
That day,

479
00:27:18,030 --> 00:27:19,310
I was with Gu Han.

480
00:27:28,030 --> 00:27:29,860
Since Xiangxiang got accepted
by The Starry Sky,

481
00:27:29,860 --> 00:27:30,710
we should celebrate.

482
00:27:30,710 --> 00:27:31,360
Our treat.

483
00:27:31,790 --> 00:27:32,710
No way.

484
00:27:32,920 --> 00:27:34,440
This is big news
for our campus TV station.

485
00:27:34,440 --> 00:27:35,990
We should be the ones paying.

486
00:27:35,990 --> 00:27:36,440
No need.

487
00:27:36,440 --> 00:27:37,960
Xiangxiang is good friends
with our basketball team.

488
00:27:37,960 --> 00:27:38,550
We'll treat.

489
00:27:38,550 --> 00:27:40,360
Xiangxiang is from
our campus TV station.

490
00:27:40,360 --> 00:27:41,920
This is our station's great milestone.

491
00:27:41,920 --> 00:27:43,200
It wouldn't be appropriate
if we don't treat.

492
00:27:43,200 --> 00:27:43,680
It's on us, it's on us.

493
00:27:43,680 --> 00:27:44,790
Don't be polite with us.

494
00:27:44,790 --> 00:27:45,470
Don't move. I've got it.

495
00:27:45,470 --> 00:27:47,310
Don't move. Let me, I've got it.

496
00:27:47,710 --> 00:27:48,370
I'll get it.

497
00:27:59,010 --> 00:28:00,080
[Round 1]

498
00:27:59,540 --> 00:28:00,550
One round to decide.

499
00:28:00,190 --> 00:28:00,450
[Fight]

500
00:28:00,550 --> 00:28:01,840
-No backing out. Winner pays. Deal.
-Okay.

501
00:28:01,840 --> 00:28:02,310
Beat him! Beat him!

502
00:28:02,310 --> 00:28:03,200
-No objections.
-You're gonna lose.

503
00:28:03,200 --> 00:28:04,200
-Fang Yu.
-Captain, come on!

504
00:28:04,200 --> 00:28:05,540
Make a move, Fang Yu.

505
00:28:05,920 --> 00:28:06,640
-Left! Left!
-Down, down, down!

506
00:28:06,640 --> 00:28:07,770
-Down, down!
-kick!

507
00:28:08,400 --> 00:28:09,200
Yes, yes, yes! Down, down!

508
00:28:09,200 --> 00:28:10,200
-Up, up, up!
-Jump, jump, jump!

509
00:28:10,200 --> 00:28:11,610
Watch your back. Combo.

510
00:28:11,920 --> 00:28:13,070
-Captain, defend!
-Jump!

511
00:28:13,070 --> 00:28:13,680
Hurry, hurry, hurry.

512
00:28:13,680 --> 00:28:15,080
Just like that! Beat him!

513
00:28:15,230 --> 00:28:16,230
Combo. This combo.

514
00:28:16,230 --> 00:28:16,880
-Defend!
-Yeah.

515
00:28:16,880 --> 00:28:17,600
-Down, down, down!
-Up!

516
00:28:17,600 --> 00:28:18,470
Crouch, crouch, crouch!

517
00:28:18,470 --> 00:28:19,440
Crouch, crouch!

518
00:28:19,440 --> 00:28:20,230
Crouch quick!

519
00:28:20,230 --> 00:28:21,040
Wait.

520
00:28:21,070 --> 00:28:21,840
Beautiful!

521
00:28:22,310 --> 00:28:23,370
We won. I'll go pay.

522
00:28:23,400 --> 00:28:24,370
Let's go, let's go, let's go.

523
00:28:24,370 --> 00:28:25,070
Bro.

524
00:28:25,200 --> 00:28:27,020
Give us a chance to pay next time.

525
00:28:27,120 --> 00:28:27,710
Okay.

526
00:28:33,270 --> 00:28:34,930
Take good care of Xiangxiang.

527
00:28:36,200 --> 00:28:37,000
Wait a minute.

528
00:28:44,550 --> 00:28:46,010
What are you trying to say?

529
00:28:48,790 --> 00:28:50,750
You still like Xiangxiang, right?

530
00:28:55,400 --> 00:28:56,920
I've known her since we were kids.

531
00:28:56,920 --> 00:28:58,380
We're childhood friends.

532
00:28:58,630 --> 00:29:00,690
That's why I did those things for her.

533
00:29:01,790 --> 00:29:02,850
Don't get me wrong.

534
00:29:03,360 --> 00:29:05,090
I hope you take good care of her.

535
00:29:10,070 --> 00:29:11,270
She likes you too.

536
00:29:18,880 --> 00:29:20,740
You're the one Xiangxiang likes.

537
00:29:21,030 --> 00:29:23,070
I really don't know why you're hesitating.

538
00:29:23,070 --> 00:29:25,270
Sometimes I get frustrated for you two.

539
00:29:29,470 --> 00:29:30,800
But that day, you two...

540
00:29:31,200 --> 00:29:32,000
Aren't you...

541
00:29:32,860 --> 00:29:34,010
That night,

542
00:29:34,550 --> 00:29:37,150
she just wanted to save me
from embarrassment.

543
00:29:37,560 --> 00:29:39,420
We cleared things up afterwards.

544
00:29:40,310 --> 00:29:42,640
We're just senior‑junior, good friends.

545
00:29:43,270 --> 00:29:44,200
Actually, I guessed a long time ago

546
00:29:44,200 --> 00:29:46,460
that the person Xiangxiang likes is you.

547
00:29:46,470 --> 00:29:48,200
After that group dinner,

548
00:29:48,510 --> 00:29:50,270
I saw her crying over you.

549
00:29:51,160 --> 00:29:53,290
That confirmed exactly how she feels.

550
00:29:55,200 --> 00:29:55,930
Understand?

551
00:30:08,360 --> 00:30:08,960
Gu Han.

552
00:30:11,920 --> 00:30:14,120
Since when did you fall for Xiangxiang?

553
00:30:24,240 --> 00:30:25,300
Since we were kids.

554
00:31:02,130 --> 00:31:07,420
♪ Time spins in circles,
running in place ♪

555
00:31:09,320 --> 00:31:13,840
♪ We once met, then passed each other by ♪

556
00:31:14,130 --> 00:31:22,850
♪ I want you to say those words at last ♪

557
00:31:23,700 --> 00:31:28,210
♪ Love means being with you ♪

558
00:31:28,660 --> 00:31:31,810
♪ I love you ♪

559
00:31:32,040 --> 00:31:35,900
♪ I miss you ♪

560
00:31:36,100 --> 00:31:43,280
♪ The me who met you that day
belongs to long, long ago ♪

561
00:31:43,600 --> 00:31:46,780
♪ Across the sea of time ♪

562
00:31:47,200 --> 00:31:51,710
♪ Reunited,
love finds its sweetest scene ♪

563
00:31:51,840 --> 00:31:58,060
♪ Loving you, I'll never change ♪

564
00:31:53,510 --> 00:31:54,120
Hello?

565
00:31:54,310 --> 00:31:55,200
Hello, Captain.

566
00:31:55,200 --> 00:31:57,360
It's my birthday tonight. Any thoughts?

567
00:31:57,360 --> 00:31:58,160
Tonight,

568
00:31:58,600 --> 00:32:01,200
I'll make the arrangements
for your birthday.

569
00:32:10,510 --> 00:32:13,440
He said he'll make the arrangements
for my birthday.

570
00:32:13,440 --> 00:32:15,270
Since when does he care so much about you?

571
00:32:15,270 --> 00:32:15,850
Right.

572
00:32:15,870 --> 00:32:17,070
I have no idea either.

573
00:32:20,790 --> 00:32:21,550
You're back.

574
00:32:22,440 --> 00:32:23,570
Xiangxiang, quick!

575
00:32:23,670 --> 00:32:25,170
Quick! Get ready!

576
00:32:25,710 --> 00:32:26,360
Ready for what?

577
00:32:26,360 --> 00:32:27,550
We're going to karaoke later.

578
00:32:27,550 --> 00:32:28,950
Hurry up and get dressed.

579
00:32:29,120 --> 00:32:29,750
Here, try this on.

580
00:32:29,750 --> 00:32:30,880
It's your boyfriend's birthday.

581
00:32:30,880 --> 00:32:31,880
Why should I dress up?

582
00:32:31,880 --> 00:32:32,920
I heard from Li Sirui

583
00:32:32,920 --> 00:32:35,160
that tonight's event
was arranged by Gu Han.

584
00:32:35,160 --> 00:32:36,160
Aren't you going?

585
00:32:37,200 --> 00:32:38,680
Hurry up and try on clothes.

586
00:32:38,680 --> 00:32:40,510
Dress our Xiangxiang up.

587
00:32:40,510 --> 00:32:41,270
Come on!

588
00:32:41,550 --> 00:32:42,230
Here.

589
00:32:42,710 --> 00:32:43,970
Take a look at this one.

590
00:32:44,230 --> 00:32:45,710
I'm not going later.

591
00:32:45,710 --> 00:32:47,510
My boyfriend is coming to see me.

592
00:32:50,310 --> 00:32:51,030
Alright.

593
00:32:51,030 --> 00:32:52,120
Right, perfume.

594
00:32:53,790 --> 00:32:55,990
This one smells good. Give me your hand.

595
00:33:00,750 --> 00:33:02,410
Does it smell like first love?

596
00:33:03,470 --> 00:33:05,200
Hurry up. Which outfit?

597
00:33:06,880 --> 00:33:07,990
I like this outfit.

598
00:33:08,440 --> 00:33:09,070
This one.

599
00:33:16,030 --> 00:33:16,960
Happy birthday.

600
00:33:16,960 --> 00:33:18,310
Hello.

601
00:33:18,310 --> 00:33:19,120
Happy birthday.

602
00:33:19,120 --> 00:33:20,200
-Happy birthday.
-Thank you.

603
00:33:20,200 --> 00:33:20,790
Thank you.

604
00:33:20,790 --> 00:33:21,470
Thank you.

605
00:33:21,920 --> 00:33:22,880
Have a seat.

606
00:33:22,880 --> 00:33:23,750
Have a seat.

607
00:33:27,270 --> 00:33:28,600
Here, have some water first.

608
00:33:28,600 --> 00:33:29,660
Thanks for coming.

609
00:33:31,030 --> 00:33:31,680
For you.

610
00:33:31,680 --> 00:33:32,270
Thanks.

611
00:33:32,270 --> 00:33:33,730
You guys look great today.

612
00:33:33,920 --> 00:33:35,310
Xiangxiang,
help yourself to whatever you want.

613
00:33:35,310 --> 00:33:36,600
-Okay.
-Here, have this.

614
00:33:36,600 --> 00:33:37,510
-Here.
-Thank you.

615
00:33:37,510 --> 00:33:38,120
It's cold.

616
00:33:39,160 --> 00:33:39,880
Thanks.

617
00:33:40,640 --> 00:33:41,310
Thank you.

618
00:33:46,750 --> 00:33:47,360
Sirui.

619
00:33:48,680 --> 00:33:50,310
-What took you so long?
-Happy birthday.

620
00:33:50,310 --> 00:33:50,790
Thank you.

621
00:33:50,790 --> 00:33:51,960
You're always the last to arrive.

622
00:33:51,960 --> 00:33:53,160
Take a penalty drink.

623
00:33:53,200 --> 00:33:53,790
Come on.

624
00:33:53,790 --> 00:33:54,750
-Here.
-Thank you.

625
00:33:54,750 --> 00:33:55,750
Not bad, Kong Fang.

626
00:33:55,750 --> 00:33:56,960
Hurry up. Bottoms up.

627
00:33:56,960 --> 00:33:58,440
Xiaotao, I want that one.

628
00:33:58,960 --> 00:33:59,820
-Sirui.
-Here.

629
00:34:01,640 --> 00:34:02,470
Happy birthday.

630
00:34:02,470 --> 00:34:03,470
Thank you.

631
00:34:03,640 --> 00:34:04,470
Help yourself.

632
00:34:04,470 --> 00:34:05,070
Okay.

633
00:34:08,510 --> 00:34:09,190
Getting anxious?

634
00:34:09,190 --> 00:34:09,960
I'll open a bottle for you.

635
00:34:09,960 --> 00:34:11,469
What would I be anxious about?

636
00:34:11,469 --> 00:34:12,440
Aren't you?

637
00:34:14,290 --> 00:34:15,330
This is good.

638
00:34:16,110 --> 00:34:16,719
Sorry.

639
00:34:17,670 --> 00:34:18,699
-Captain.
-I bought a cake.

640
00:34:18,699 --> 00:34:19,380
I'm late.

641
00:34:19,510 --> 00:34:20,630
-Thank you, captain.
-Come on, captain.

642
00:34:20,630 --> 00:34:22,090
-Put it here.
-Blueberry.

643
00:34:22,190 --> 00:34:22,800
Yes.

644
00:34:24,760 --> 00:34:26,690
How about we all have a drink first?

645
00:34:26,800 --> 00:34:28,460
-Come on.
-Let's have a drink.

646
00:34:28,840 --> 00:34:30,639
-Cheers.
-Thank you for coming.

647
00:34:32,150 --> 00:34:32,920
Sirui.
